In this deck every creature is a burn spell. Kreat deals 1 damage to each opponent whenever another creature enters under your control — tokens included — so Siege-Gang Commander is four damage to every opponent before it does anything else, and a Krenko activation is as much damage as it makes Goblins. Stack more cards that do the same thing and each creature does more: with Impact Tremors, Purphoros, Agate Instigator, Molten Gatekeeper and Witty Roastmaster all out, one 1/1 entering is 7 damage to every opponent.
Only creatures YOU control count. Tokens you hand an opponent — from Tempt with Vengeance — trigger nothing.
That also makes every infinite-creature loop an infinite-damage loop: with Kreat out, each copy entering is 1 damage to each opponent. The deck has four of them — see the combos.

# The commander
General Kreat, the Boltbringer :: three mana. Whenever another creature enters under your control, 1 damage to each opponent. Whenever your Goblins attack, a 1/1 Goblin joins the attack — which is another creature entering, so another ping.
Lightning Greaves :: shroud the turn Kreat lands, and haste so Krenko, Mob Boss can tap the turn it lands. Never equip it to Kiki-Jiki — shroud stops Zealous Conscripts or Restoration Angel from targeting Kiki.
Swiftfoot Boots :: the second copy.
Hexing Squelcher :: every other creature you control has "ward — pay 2 life," and your spells can't be countered.
Deflecting Swat :: free with Kreat out; send their removal somewhere harmless.
Pyroblast :: one mana to counter the blue spell aimed at your combo, or destroy a blue permanent.
Red Elemental Blast :: the same, a second time.

# Infinite combos — from turn 6
Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker + Zealous Conscripts :: Kiki copies Conscripts, and the copy's enter trigger untaps Kiki — target Kiki itself. Repeat for as many hasty 3/3s as you want, the same turn Kiki lands (it has haste). With Kreat out every copy entering is 1 damage to each opponent, so the loop wins on the spot. Never leave Lightning Greaves on Kiki: shroud stops the Conscripts copy targeting it.
Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker + Lightning Crafter + Goblin Bombardment :: Kiki copies the Crafter. The copy's champion trigger exiles Kiki; the hasty copy taps for 3 damage; sacrifice it to Goblin Bombardment; Kiki returns untapped — it has haste — and copies the Crafter again. Unlimited 3-damage shots, so this one kills on its own. Skirk Prospector work as the outlet too. The original Crafter must stay on the battlefield; when it enters you must exile another Goblin or Shaman (champion) or sacrifice it.
Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker + Thornbite Staff + Goblin Bombardment :: the Staff attaches itself to Kiki when Kiki enters after it (otherwise equip costs {4}). Kiki copies any nonlegendary creature, you sacrifice a creature to Goblin Bombardment, and the death untaps Kiki. Unlimited loops. Every copy entering is also a Kreat ping.
Goblin Recruiter -> Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker + Conspicuous Snoop :: Recruiter puts Kiki on TOP of your library. Snoop has every activated ability of the Goblin on top, so it copies itself with Kiki's ability — and every hasty copy does the same. Snoop needs haste or a turn in play to start, and most copies end up tapped, so finish with Kreat's pings — every copy entering is 1 damage to each opponent. Rundvelt Hordemaster exiles your top card whenever a Goblin dies, so don't let one die while Kiki sits on top. Outside the combo, Snoop lets you cast Goblins straight off the top of your library.
Krenko, Mob Boss + Thornbite Staff + Skirk Prospector :: equip the Staff to Krenko ({4} — he's a Warrior, so it won't attach itself). Krenko taps for a Goblin per Goblin; sacrifice one to Skirk Prospector; the death untaps Krenko; tap again. The army doubles every lap. Win with Kreat: every new Goblin is 1 damage to each opponent.
Dualcaster Mage + Twinflame :: in your main phase, cast Twinflame on any creature you control, then flash Dualcaster in with Twinflame still on the stack. Dualcaster copies Twinflame onto itself; that hasty token copies it again; repeat. Unlimited hasty 2/2s, each one a Kreat ping.

# Tutor lines — what to fetch, and when
Goblin Matron -> Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker :: when you already hold Zealous Conscripts, Lightning Crafter or the Staff — Kiki is the piece that turns half a combo into a kill.
Goblin Matron -> Goblin Recruiter :: when you're missing two or more pieces. Matron gets Recruiter; Recruiter stacks the rest on top of your library.
Goblin Matron -> Krenko, Mob Boss :: when Thornbite Staff is already out, or when you simply need a board this turn.
Goblin Matron -> Lightning Crafter :: when Kiki-Jiki is on the battlefield and you have a free outlet — the Crafter is the last piece.
Goblin Matron -> Skirk Prospector :: when the combo is assembled but nothing will sacrifice for free.
Imperial Recruiter -> Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker :: power 2, so the one non-Goblin tutor that still finds Kiki. It also gets Dualcaster Mage when you hold Twinflame, or Goblin Recruiter, Conspicuous Snoop or Skirk Prospector.
Gamble -> Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker :: any card — usually Kiki, the Staff or Goblin Recruiter, whichever has no backup. Cast it with a full hand: the random discard is then less likely to hit the card you just fetched.
Goblin Engineer -> Thornbite Staff :: puts the Staff into your graveyard, then {R}, tap and sacrifice another artifact puts it onto the battlefield. Engineer needs a turn or haste before it can tap.
Goblin Recruiter -> Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker + Lightning Crafter + Skirk Prospector :: without Snoop, stack the missing pieces with the one you need first on top. Recruiter only arranges your library — Goblin Ringleader, Conspicuous Snoop or your draws reach it — so unless something reaches it this turn, cast it the turn before you go off, not on curve.
Goblin Ringleader :: every Goblin in your top four goes to your hand — the cleanest way to cash in a Recruiter stack.

# Goblin Recruiter setups — what to stack, top card first
Goblin Recruiter -> Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker :: with Conspicuous Snoop able to tap — every Snoop copy entering is a Kreat ping. Don't let a Goblin die while Kiki sits on top: Rundvelt Hordemaster would exile it.
Goblin Recruiter -> Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker -> Lightning Crafter -> Skirk Prospector -> Goblin Warchief :: then cast Muxus: all four enter at once — four Kreat pings — and the Crafter champions Recruiter, so Kiki can start copying it immediately.
Goblin Recruiter -> Siege-Gang Commander -> Krenko, Mob Boss -> Goblin Matron -> Goblin Chieftain :: the refill for Goblin Ringleader; every one of them is several Kreat pings.
Anything that searches your library shuffles it and wrecks the stack — Goblin Matron, Imperial Recruiter and Gamble. Use those before Recruiter, never after.

# Every creature is damage
Impact Tremors :: 1 more to each opponent per creature.
Purphoros, God of the Forge :: 2 more to each opponent per creature. Indestructible, and only a creature once your devotion to red reaches five.
Agate Instigator :: 1 more per creature. Pay offspring ({1}{R} extra) and you get a 1/1 copy that does it too.
Molten Gatekeeper :: 1 more per creature, and unearth brings it back for {R}.
Witty Roastmaster :: 1 more per creature.
Roaming Throne :: name Goblin. Kreat is a Goblin, so both of its triggers happen twice — 2 damage per creature and two tokens per attack. It doubles every Goblin that makes tokens when it enters or attacks, too: Siege-Gang Commander makes six.

# Making Goblins
Krenko, Mob Boss :: taps for a 1/1 for every Goblin you control — the army doubles every turn, and each one is a ping. Give it haste and it goes the turn it lands.
Krenko, Tin Street Kingpin :: each attack puts a +1/+1 counter on it, then makes Goblins equal to its power — two the first time, three the next.
Siege-Gang Commander :: three Goblins when it enters, and {1}{R} sacrifices one for 2 damage.
Beetleback Chief :: two Goblins when it enters.
Siege-Gang Lieutenant :: two hasty Goblins each of your combats while Kreat is on the battlefield; {2} sacrifices one for 1 damage.
Legion Warboss :: a hasty Goblin each of your combats.
Howlsquad Heavy :: a Goblin each of your combats, and every other Goblin has haste.
Squee, Dubious Monarch :: an attacking Goblin every time it attacks, and it recasts itself from the graveyard.
Goblin Instigator :: two bodies for two mana.
Mogg War Marshal :: a Goblin when it enters and another when it dies.
Muxus, Goblin Grandee :: puts every Goblin with mana value 5 or less from your top six straight onto the battlefield.
Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker :: taps each turn for a hasty copy of your best creature — Siege-Gang Commander is four creatures entering every turn.
Fable of the Mirror-Breaker :: a Goblin that makes Treasure when it attacks, then a card filter, then Reflection of Kiki-Jiki — a copy maker that costs {1} each use and needs a turn before it can tap.
Krenko's Command :: the same.
Tempt with Vengeance :: X hasty 1/1s. Each opponent may take X too; for each one who does, you get X more. Their tokens can attack you, so only the numbers decide whether it's worth it.

# Payoffs
Goblin Bombardment :: sacrifice a creature for 1 damage anywhere. It turns every token into reach.
Pashalik Mons :: 1 damage whenever one of your Goblins dies; {3}{R} and a sacrifice make two new Goblins — two more pings.
Hobgoblin Bandit Lord :: other Goblins +1/+1, and {R} with a tap deals damage equal to the number of Goblins that entered this turn.
Shared Animosity :: every attacking Goblin gets +1/+0 for each other attacking Goblin. Goblins that enter already attacking don't get the bonus, but they raise everyone else's.
Goblin Chieftain :: other Goblins +1/+1 and haste.
Goblin Warchief :: Goblins cost one less and have haste.
Rundvelt Hordemaster :: other Goblins +1/+1; whenever a Goblin dies, the top card of your library is exiled, and if it's a Goblin creature you can cast it until the end of your next turn. Careful: it exiles your top card whenever a Goblin dies, so once Kiki-Jiki is stacked on top for the Snoop combo, don't let a Goblin die first.
Goblin Trashmaster :: other Goblins +1/+1; sacrifice a Goblin to destroy an artifact.
Goblin Lackey :: a turn-one play that cheats a Goblin in when it connects.
Valakut, the Molten Pinnacle :: once you control five other Mountains, every Mountain you play is 3 damage anywhere.

# Cards and mana
The One Ring :: cast it for protection from everything until your next turn, then draw more every turn.
Skullclamp :: equip it to a creature with 1 toughness and it dies: two cards for one mana. A lord that adds toughness keeps your tokens alive, so pick an X/1.
Wheel of Fortune :: everyone draws seven, you included.
Jeska's Will :: with Kreat out, both halves: a red mana per card in an opponent's hand and the top three cards to play.
Brightstone Ritual :: a red mana for every Goblin on the battlefield.
Skirk Prospector :: sacrifice a Goblin for {R}.
Sol Ring :: the fastest start.
Arcane Signet :: a second rock.
Ruby Medallion :: red spells cost {1} less — generic mana only, so a one-mana {R} spell still costs {R}.
The Fire Crystal :: red spells cost one less and every creature you control has haste.
Patchwork Banner :: name Goblin: +1/+1, and it taps for mana.
Three Tree City :: name Goblin: {2} and a tap make a red mana for every Goblin you control.
Cavern of Souls :: name Goblin: they can't be countered.
Arena of Glory :: {R}, tap and exert it for {R}{R} — one extra mana — and a creature spell cast with it gains haste.
Castle Embereth :: {1}{R}{R}: your creatures get +1/+0.
Den of the Bugbear :: a land that attacks as a 3/2 Goblin and makes an attacking token.
Sokenzan, Crucible of Defiance :: channel it for two hasty 1/1s — two pings.
Nykthos, Shrine to Nyx :: mono-red devotion into a pile of red mana.
War Room :: {3}, tap it and pay 1 life: draw a card.

# Answers
Lightning Bolt :: 3 damage for one mana.
Abrade :: 3 damage or an artifact destroyed.
Untimely Malfunction :: destroys an artifact, redirects a single-target spell, or stops two blockers.
Fiery Confluence :: three modes, repeats allowed: 2 damage to each opponent three times is 6 each.
Chaos Warp :: the red answer to anything.
Vandalblast :: overloaded, every artifact they control.
Sundering Eruption :: a land when you need one; late, destroy a land and stop every creature without flying from blocking for a combat kill.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep two or three lands and two-drops that make bodies. Kreat lands on turn three; from then on every creature is damage.
Deploy the pingers before the token spells. Siege-Gang Commander is 4 damage with Kreat alone and 20 with Impact Tremors, Purphoros and Agate Instigator out.
Krenko, Mob Boss needs haste to tap the turn it lands: have Goblin Warchief, Goblin Chieftain, Howlsquad Heavy, The Fire Crystal or Greaves ready. Kiki-Jiki has haste already.
Red has little protection. Against a sweeper, sacrifice to Goblin Bombardment or Skirk Prospector in response — every death still counts for Pashalik Mons.
